{"type":"text","timestamp":1770256622946,"sessionID":"ses_3d47c9827ffeQjEDFsZ3r82xqr","part":{"id":"prt_c2b845e19001SHYPgvVDfIREuC","sessionID":"ses_3d47c9827ffeQjEDFsZ3r82xqr","messageID":"msg_c2b8448b4001CM9aaCW1t3z5YE","type":"text","text":"I have implemented the `ContactForm` component in `app/ContactForm.tsx` with an inline server action as requested.\n\nThe implementation includes:\n1.  An **inline server action** `submitContact` defined directly within the component.\n2.  **JavaScript validation** within the server action to ensure `name`, `email`, and `message` are present.\n3.  Basic HTML structure and styling for the form.\n\nYou can find the implementation in `app/ContactForm.tsx`:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function ContactForm() {\n  async function submitContact(formData: FormData) {\n    'use server'\n    \n    const name = formData.get('name')\n    const email = formData.get('email')\n    const message = formData.get('message')\n\n    // JavaScript validation in the server action\n    if (!name || !email || !message) {\n      throw new Error('All fields are required')\n    }\n    \n    // In a real application, you would save the data or send an email here\n    console.log('Form submitted:', { name, email, message })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h2>Contact Us</h2>\n      <form action={submitContact} style={{ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: '10px', maxWidth: '400px' }}>\n        {/* Form fields... */}\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```","time":{"start":1770256622945,"end":1770256622945},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}}
